"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative aimed at revolutionizing the company's approach to the field. It was introduced by Alex with Sarah Tan as the lead, starting with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000. The project has progressed through several phases, including design, testing, and development, with Omar Jensen leading the development phase. The team recently celebrated the successful completion of the testing phase and the achievement of the first major milestone ahead of schedule, which involved a successfully tested prototype for secure file sharing. The budget was initially adjusted to $550,000 to cover unforeseen expenses and real-time analytics integration, but was later approved by the executive board for a total of $2M to cover research, development, and marketing. The team has expanded to include Mike Chen and Lisa Ray for machine learning and cloud computing expertise. Future plans include user interface enhancements in October, security protocol updates (multi-factor authentication and encryption) effective January next year, and exploring a partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology."
